              "content": "# REPO / FOLIO\n\nSelf-updating portfolio site generated from a GitHub profile.\nRust + axum backend, vanilla frontend, Docker deploy.\n\nThe page never needs manual editing: repositories, stars, topics and language\nstatistics are pulled from the GitHub REST API by a background task, cached in\nmemory (and on disk), and pushed to the browser without a reload.\n\n---\n\n## Contents\n\n- [How it works](#how-it-works)\n- [Quick start](#quick-start)\n- [Docker](#docker)\n- [Configuration](#configuration)\n- [API](#api)\n- [Design concept](#design-concept)\n- [Project layout](#project-layout)\n- [Testing & quality](#testing--quality)\n- [Assumptions](#assumptions)\n\n---\n\n## How it works\n\n```\nGitHub REST API\n     │  conditional GET (If-None-Match / ETag)\n     ▼\nrefresh task (tokio, every REFRESH_INTERVAL_SECS)\n     │  normalize → filter pins/exclusions → aggregate languages\n     ▼\ncache: Arc<RwLock<Snapshot>> + JSON file on disk\n     │\n     ├── GET /api/profile   ─┐\n     ├── GET /api/repos     ─┼─→ browser (vanilla JS polls every 30s)\n     └── GET /              ─┘    list updates in place, no reload\n```\n\nRefresh cycle:\n\n1. `GET /users/{user}` — conditional.\n2. `GET /users/{user}/repos?per_page=100&sort=full_name&type=owner` — **每个 page**\n   is validated with its own ETag (a `304` on page 1 does not stop us from\n   checking page 2), so a new repository on a later page is still picked up.\n3. `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/languages` for repositories whose breakdown is\n   missing or whose `updated_at` changed — at most `LANGUAGE_BUDGET` per cycle,\n   so a large account cannot burn the rate limit at once. Missing repositories\n   are filled in over subsequent cycles.\n\nGuarantees:\n\n- **Errors never destroy data.** On any failure the last good snapshot keeps\n  being served (`stale: true` in the API), and the error is logged.\n- **Rate limits are respected.** `403`/`429` with rate-limit headers put the\n  client into a cooldown until `x-ratelimit-reset` / `retry-after`, so a\n  refresh cycle stops instead of hammering GitHub.\n- **Cold start is instant.** The disk snapshot is loaded at boot; if it belongs\n  to another `GITHUB_USERNAME` it is ignored.\n- **Pins survive config changes.** Raw payloads are cached, so editing\n  `PINNED_REPOS`/`EXCLUDED_REPOS` and restarting re-applies them without\n  re-downloading.\n\n---\n\n## Quick start\n\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env      # set at least GITHUB_USERNAME\ncargo run\n# → http://localhost:8080\n```\n\nRequirements: Rust stable (1.88+). A `GITHUB_TOKEN` is optional but raises the\nrate limit from 60 to 5000 requests/hour.\n\n```bash\nADMIN_TOKEN=secret cargo run\ncurl -X POST localhost:8080/api/refresh -H 'x-admin-token: secret'\n```\n\n## Docker\n\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env\ndocker compose up -d --build\ndocker compose logs -f\n```\n\n- Multi-stage build: `rust:slim-bookworm` → `debian:bookworm-slim`.\n- Dependency compilation is cached via BuildKit cache mounts (`--mount=type=cache`).\n- Runs as UID/GID `10001`, `read_only` root filesystem, all capabilities dropped.\n- `HEALTHCHECK` hits `/health`; the named volume `portfolio-cache` keeps `data/cache.json`\n  between restarts.\n- `stop_grace_period: 30s` gives the refresher time to flush the final snapshot.\n\nWithout Compose:\n\n```bash\ndocker build -t repo-folio .\ndocker run -d --name folio -p 8080:8080 \\\n  -e GITHUB_USERNAME=octocat -e ADMIN_TOKEN=secret \\\n  -v folio-data:/data repo-folio\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n| Variable | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `GITHUB_USERNAME` | **required** | Profile to build the site from (user or org). |\n| `GITHUB_TOKEN` | — | Optional PAT; only raises the rate limit. Never sent to the browser. |\n| `REFRESH_INTERVAL_SECS` | `300` | Background refresh period (1 … 2592000). |\n| `PORT` | `8080` | HTTP port. |\n| `ADMIN_TOKEN` | — | Unset ⇒ `POST /api/refresh` returns `401`. Use 32+ random chars. |\n| `PINNED_REPOS` | — | Comma separated `name` or `owner/name`; shown first, in this order. |\n| `EXCLUDED_REPOS` | — | Comma separated; hidden everywhere, including statistics. |\n| `SHOW_FORKS` | `false` | Default visibility of forks (overridable per request). |\n| `SHOW_ARCHIVED` | `false` | Default visibility of archived repositories. |\n| `CACHE_FILE` | `data/cache.json` | Snapshot path. Empty or `none` disables persistence. |\n| `LANGUAGE_BUDGET` | `40` | Max `/languages` requests per refresh cycle. |\n| `GITHUB_API_BASE` | `https://api.github.com` | Override for GHES or tests. |\n| `CORS_ALLOW_ORIGIN` | — | Exact origin for cross-origin reads; same-origin only by default. |\n| `RUST_LOG` | `github_portfolio=info,…` | `tracing` filter. |\n| `LOG_FORMAT` | pretty | `json` for structured logs (Docker sets this). |\n\n## API\n\nAll error bodies are `{\"error\": \"...\", \"code\": \"...\"}`, with codes such as\n`cache_cold`, `unauthorized`, `github_rate_limited`, `config_error`.\n\n### `GET /api/profile`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"profile\": {\n    \"login\": \"octocat\", \"name\": \"The Octocat\", \"avatar_url\": \"https://…\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/octocat\", \"bio\": \"…\", \"location\": \"…\",\n    \"blog\": \"https://…\", \"twitter_username\": \"octocat\", \"company\": \"@github\",\n    \"followers\": 12345, \"following\": 9, \"public_repos\": 8\n  },\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-01T10:00:00Z\",\n  \"repo_count\": 8,\n  \"stale\": false\n}\n```\n\n`503 cache_cold` until the first successful fetch.\n\n### `GET /api/repos`\n\nQuery parameters (all optional): `q`, `language`, `topic`,\n`sort=stars|updated|name`, `show_forks=true|false`, `show_archived=true|false`.\nUnknown `sort` values silently fall back to `stars`. Pinned repositories always\ncome first in `PINNED_REPOS` order, then the requested sort applies.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"repos\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 1296269, \"name\": \"Hello-World\", \"full_name\": \"octocat/Hello-World\",\n      \"description\": \"My first repository on GitHub!\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/octocat/Hello-World\",\n      \"homepage\": \"https://hello.example\",\n      \"language\": \"Rust\", \"stargazers_count\": 2400, \"forks_count\": 1900,\n      \"topics\": [\"cli\", \"system-design\"], \"updated_at\": \"2024-04-30T12:00:00Z\",\n      \"fork\": false, \"archived\": false, \"pinned\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"languages\": [{ \"name\": \"Rust\", \"bytes\": 10000, \"color\": \"#dea584\" }],\n  \"available_languages\": [\"HTML\", \"Rust\", \"TypeScript\"],\n  \"available_topics\": [\"cli\", \"observability\"],\n  \"total\": 3,\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-01T10:00:00Z\",\n  \"stale\": false,\n  \"languages_complete\": true,\n  \"defaults\": { \"show_forks\": false, \"show_archived\": false }\n}\n```\n\n`languages` is aggregated from every repository's `/languages` bytes.\n`languages_complete: false` means some breakdowns are still loading (large\naccounts fill in over several cycles).\n\n### `POST /api/refresh`\n\nRequires `x-admin-token: <ADMIN_TOKEN>` (or `Authorization: Bearer <token>`),\ncompared in constant time. Schedules an immediate refresh and returns `202`\nwith `{\"status\":\"scheduled\"}`; `401` if the token is missing/wrong or unset.\n\n### `GET /health` (also `GET /api/health`)\n\n```json\n{\"status\":\"ok\",\"ready\":true,\"cached\":true,\"updated_at\":\"…\",\"uptime_secs\":42,\n \"refresh_interval_secs\":300,\"user\":\"octocat\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\"}\n```\n\nAlways `200` while the process can answer, so a GitHub outage never restarts a\nhealthy container. Use `ready` for readiness checks.\n\n### Other routes\n\n`GET /` page, `GET /app.css`, `GET /app.js`, `GET /favicon.svg`,\n`GET /robots.txt`. The frontend is embedded into the binary (`include_str!`).\n\nBoth API endpoints emit `ETag` and honor `If-None-Match` (`304`), so polling is\ncheap.\n\n## Design concept\n\n**Editorial print, not dashboard.** The site reads like a small design journal:\nwarm cream paper (`#f4f1e8`), near-black ink (`#16170f`), and a single acid\nlime signal (`#c8f751`) plus clay (`#b4462b`) for accents. Lime is the \"alive\"\ncolor — theme icon, pinned cards, hover underlines — so freshness of data is\nlegible at a glance.\n\n- **Type**: serif display (Iowan/Palatino/Georgia stack) for names and headings\n  to give it a printed feel, monospace for metadata, labels, star counts and\n  repository names — a deliberate nod to code. Body text stays in the system UI\n  stack for comfortable reading. No web fonts, so the page never shifts.\n- **Structure**: a sticky left profile column and a fluid card grid on the\n  right; on mobile it collapses to one column with the profile first.\n- **Motion**: short, purposeful transitions (cards lift 3px, underline grows,\n  language bars animate once), all disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n- **Accessibility**: semantic landmarks, a skip link, visible focus rings on\n  every control, `aria-live` status for counts and sync state, alt text built\n  from real data, and WCAG-AA-ish contrast in both themes.\n- **Themes**: follows `prefers-color-scheme`, with a manual toggle persisted in\n  `localStorage`; the dark theme is a true warm-black, not a blue-gray inversion.\n- **States**: skeleton shimmer while loading, dashed empty state with a reset\n  button, and a warning banner when the server serves a stale snapshot.\n\n## Project layout\n\n```\n.\n├── Cargo.toml\n├── Cargo.lock\n├── Dockerfile\n├── docker-compose.yml\n├── .dockerignore\n├── .env.example\n├── Makefile\n├── src\n│   ├── main.rs          binary: logging, cache warm-up, refresher, shutdown\n│   ├── lib.rs           crate root\n│   ├── config.rs        env parsing + validation\n│   ├── error.rs         AppError → HTTP mapping\n│   ├── state.rs         AppState, RefreshOutcome\n│   ├── cache.rs         in-memory + JSON snapshot cache\n│   ├── refresh.rs       GitHub → snapshot pipeline\n│   ├── filters.rs       filtering, sorting, facets\n│   ├── colors.rs        language palette\n│   ├── util.rs          formatting helpers\n│   ├── models\n│   │   ├── mod.rs\n│   │   ├── github.rs    GitHub REST payloads\n│   │   └── snapshot.rs  normalized domain models\n│   ├── github\n│   │   ├── mod.rs\n│   │   ├── client.rs    conditional GET, pagination, rate limits\n│   │   └── error.rs     GitHubError\n│   └── routes\n│       ├── mod.rs       router, CORS/CSP/compression layers\n│       ├── api.rs       JSON handlers\n│       ├── assets.rs    embedded static assets\n│       └── health.rs    health/readiness\n├── static\n│   ├── index.html\n│   ├── app.css\n│   ├── app.js\n│   └── favicon.svg\n└── tests\n    ├── integration.rs   end-to-end refresh via a mock GitHub server\n    └── fixtures\n        ├── user.json\n        ├── repos.json\n        └── languages.json\n```\n\n## Testing & quality\n\n```bash\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\ncargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings\ncargo test\nnode --check static/app.js\n```\n\nCovered: GitHub payload parsing (including minimal/partial payloads), filter\nand sort logic (pins, exclusions, forks, archived, facets), config parsing,\nETag generation, cache persistence/corruption, language aggregation, and — via\n`tests/integration.rs` against a mock HTTP server — cold start → `503`, first\nrefresh, `304` revalidation, a **new repository appearing after a refresh**, a\nsecond page changing while page 1 still returns `304`, ETag `304` on our own\nAPI, the failure path (snapshot retained, `stale: true`), and refresh auth.\n\nOther safety measures: no `unwrap()`/`expect()` in production paths, no\n`panic!`, redirects disabled in the HTTP client, pagination URLs validated\nagainst the API origin, repository names validated before entering a URL, and\nall remote strings rendered with `textContent` (never `innerHTML`).\n\n## Assumptions\n\nDetails that were not specified, decided as follows:\n\n1. **JSON API + vanilla frontend** instead of SSR templates — it gives live\n   updates without reloads and keeps the binary free of template compilation.\n   The trade-off: the first paint is a skeleton, then data arrives in one round\n   trip. Static assets are embedded in the binary for a minimal image.\n2. **Repositories are read from `/users/{user}/repos?type=owner`** — forks are\n   excluded by GitHub unless `SHOW_FORKS` asks for them, and the site never\n   mixes in repositories the user only contributes to.\n3. **Pinned and excluded entries are matched by `name` or `owner/name`,\n   case-insensitively**; `PINNED_REPOS` order is the display order.\n4. **Pins/exclusions are presentation, not data.** Raw payloads are cached\n   separately so config edits do not require a re-fetch.\n5. **`/api/refresh` is asynchronous** (`202 scheduled`) and coalesced with the\n   timer, so a slow GitHub response cannot hold an HTTP connection open or\n   double the rate-limit cost.\n6. **`/health` returns `200` even without cached data** (with `ready: false`),\n   so a GitHub outage does not cause a container restart loop; monitoring\n   should alert on `ready`.\n7. **Language requests are budgeted** (`LANGUAGE_BUDGET`, default 40 per cycle)\n   rather than fetched for every repository at once — this keeps a 200-repo\n   account inside the unauthenticated rate limit while still converging.\n8. **`CACHE_FILE` defaults to `data/cache.json`**; `SHOW_FORKS`/`SHOW_ARCHIVED`\n   only change defaults — the browser can override them per request.\n9. **No database.** One profile is cached per process; scaling out would need\n   sticky instances or a shared store, which is out of scope here.\n10. **Text is Russian** in the UI (the brief was written in Russian), with\n    language/monospace accents; the API is language-neutral.\n",
